The final browser suites exercise real frontend/API/PostgreSQL. Portal browser requests use actual isolated Oracle HTTP responses, not mocked acquisition payloads. Deliberate error-injection scenarios remain named. A Windows console encoding failure in a diagnostic print was corrected by UTF-8 execution; final browser JSON contains all20 PASS results. No failing product assertion was removed. Frontend build/tests completed after the Portal frontend changes; the final subsequent edits affected backend Radar only.

## Regressions discovered and corrected

The full backend gate reproduced ZIP-manifest compression-size oscillation. The release packager now stores the embedded manifest without compression, returns the exact embedded fixed-point manifest and fails on nonconvergence. Four timestamp-fraction variants verify exact archive size and returned/embedded equality.

A v5 API activation passed the initial Portal and contract gates, but an additional full-real-data Radar check timed out at120s and finished141s under the clone's0.5CPU/384MiB limits. A matched30-target/5797-listing comparison confirmed5.53s for v5 versus1.16s for the prior image. Production was safely switched back to the exact previous image; additive0022 remained. This was a confirmed regression, not an upstream Portal failure.

The final v6 computes publication identities and type-conflict facts once per detection request and groups eligible comparables once. No process-wide cache can become stale. Under identical limits, the same sample takes1.10s, with identical13 opportunity IDs, estimates and discounts across previous/v5/v6 images. Regression tests verify uncached valuation parity and facts refreshed between requests. The full Radar HTTP gate then returned200 with20 mathematically consistent rows. All final release gates were rerun as applicable before v6 activation.

## Files modified in this continuation

