## Backup, rollback and resources

Fresh protected backup:/home/ubuntu/backups/portal-final-release-20261012 (directory0700/files0600). Database dump20,541,796bytes; SHA256 `8c8c1183e456858fc2831c8861b6fe62eeeaedb63216809b6f76d3f8f25875d1`. Restored in network-none PostgreSQL; counts verified. Both final and old application read compatibility on0022 passed. Observation UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE guards remain enforced.

Rollback tag valoria-remediation-rollback:20261012 resolves to `sha256:3342a667c071319097e6c6aed23bfd03ec231f6bf44cd17434d6a0de13187f15`. An actual switch-back was executed successfully during the Radar investigation. Rollback uses the original five Compose files with PORTAL_GEO_RELEASE_IMAGE=valoria-portal-geo:0ceeb1e-20261011 and recreates API only; retain additive0022. No destructive schema downgrade or restore is required. Configuration/globals backups remain private on Oracle; inactive v5 override is preserved separately.

Final preflight had4.82GB available RAM and25.48GB free disk within the unchanged6GB Oracle Always Free VM. Temporary candidate/restore services used explicit memory/CPU limits. All five task-created Oracle test containers, their verified anonymous volumes, isolated network and local SSH tunnel were removed after verification. Protected backups and rollback/final images remain. Dedicated local candidate frontend/API/PostgreSQL/Redis remain on3003/8013/15433/16379 with workers/scheduler disabled for review.

## Remaining scope and evidence

Finding16 remains a product decision,17 has no real office coverage, and18's physical type for6842 remains unconfirmed; conservative conflict guards preserve source classification. Independent geographic truth for every listing and exhaustive race/search permutations are not claimed. Public V2 frontend publication remains a separate deployment task. These are recorded limits, with no remaining Portal/API release blocker.

The acceptance evidence directory retains baseline history, final tests,20 browser JSON results/traces/screenshots, live acquisition evidence, source manifest, image/contract gates, backup/restore/rehearsal, safety rollback, performance parity, deployment, public proxy and final cleanup proof. acceptance-evidence-sha256.json records hashes. Earlier failed screenshots/logs are investigation history; final JSON and v6 gate logs are authoritative.
